      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "A painter has to paint all four sides of a fence. Which customary unit of measurement could the painter use to quantify the volume of paint he needs for each side?",
      "worked_solution": "A table showing the customary units of volume is given below.\n\n| Name | Symbol | Conversion |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Gallon | $\\text{gal}$ | $1\\,\\text{gal}=8\\,\\text{pints}$ |\n| Pint | $\\text{pt}$ | $1\\,\\text{pt}=2\\,\\text{cups}$ |\n| Cup | $-$ | $1\\,\\text{cup}=8\\,\\text{fl oz}$ |\n| Fluid ounce | $\\text{fl oz}$ | $-$ |\n\nTherefore, from the given options, the only unit of volume is \"gallon.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
